A credential named in ci.yml, even from a step-level env, breaks the rule
that rules-alert.yml is the only workflow mentioning secrets. The on: here
is a flow mapping.
-- ci.yml --
name: ci
on: {pull_request: {}, push: {branches: [main]}}
permissions: {contents: read}
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: uses a credential
        env: {TOKEN: "${{ secrets.PUSHOVER_APP_TOKEN }}"}
        run: go test ./...
-- want --
ci.yml:9 secrets-outside-alert
